# Direct dependencies of the reranker image (see Dockerfile) and of the
# local development environment. Hash-Lock folgt spaeter -- requirements.txt
# is a plain `pip freeze` of the resolved tree, not a
# `pip-compile --generate-hashes` lock, same discipline as Weave-Tools'
# own backend/requirements.in and Weave-Retrieval/Weave-Runtime's.
#
# fastapi/uvicorn/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pytest/httpx pins are kept
# identical to Weave-Tools' backend/requirements.in -- no reason for this
# service's web-framework/test stack to drift from a sibling service's.
#
# sentence-transformers, NOT fastembed: BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3 (the model
# this service is built around) is absent from fastembed 0.8.0's
# TextCrossEncoder.list_supported_models() as of this writing -- checked
# experimentally, see README.md's "Warum nicht fastembed" for the full
# list fastembed DOES carry (6 cross-encoders, none of them this one) and
# the size/latency tradeoff this fallback costs.
#
# torch MUST come from the CPU wheel index, not plain PyPI -- the default
# PyPI `torch` wheel bundles CUDA and is ~5x larger for a service that will
# only ever run on CPU (see Dockerfile and README's "Imagegroesse"):
#
#   pip install --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu torch==2.13.0
#
fastapi==0.141.1
uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4
pydantic==2.13.5
pydantic-settings==2.15.0
httpx==0.28.1
pytest==9.1.1
sentence-transformers==6.0.1
torch==2.13.0
